Why: coordinator mailbox answer 1 (2026-11-16) authorizes this assertion-only
portability fix for locked pagable 0.4.1. ARM32 AtomicU64 alignment gives ten
words, while wasm32 retains twelve. The coordinator checked that no runtime
code depends on this size: no size_of/transmute/offset_of/from_raw_parts in
src/, and these assertions are its only [usize; N] mentions. Keep both checks;
change no runtime algorithm or dependency version. Applied to checksum-verified
external crate source, never the shared registry cache.

--- a/src/pagable_arc.rs
+++ b/src/pagable_arc.rs
@@ -739,2 +739,4 @@
-#[cfg(target_pointer_width = "32")]
+#[cfg(all(target_pointer_width = "32", not(target_arch = "arm")))]
 static_assertions::assert_eq_size!(PagableArcInner<[usize; 4]>, [usize; 12]);
+#[cfg(all(target_pointer_width = "32", target_arch = "arm"))]
